## 4. Scope audit

This theorem deliberately does **not** claim that the nested lane's partner endpoints all lie on one prescribed physical host arc. The earlier attempted shortcut from a four-block whole-boundary picture is too strong: the common hub cut places all births on one complementary boundary shore and all hubward partners on the other, whose region-label word turns once. The correct invariant is the unimodal partner-region word (NR.7).

The reversal of the `+` birth-side block is exactly what upgrades that unimodality to the nested-lane conclusion (NR.5).

No regular-shell contradiction follows from nesting alone. The remaining work is to combine the nested, coherent-sign, stress-dilute rail with the common inverse-`D` train grid and the near-central antipodal metric geometry.

---

## 5. Frontier effect

A surviving exact-antipodal high-`t` branch must contain an unbounded object with all of the following simultaneously:

```text
one complete birth-side diameter rail
+ strictly nested support intervals
+ pairwise crossing and pairwise endpoint-disjoint bars
+ pairwise disjoint growing exact-phase birth neighborhoods
+ a coherent-transverse-sign subrail of half the size
+ one common inverse-D near-triangular train grid
+ optional depth-independent B_i = O(1/D) stress quantile
+ bounded absolute local reactions.
```

The previous advancing-staircase alternative is not needed for the guaranteed lane. The next closure target can therefore be stated against a single nested support geometry.

**Disposition:** sharpened partner-rainbow unimodality to an exact full-lane nesting theorem and combined it with the current stress quantile and coherent-sign extraction. C-II and Level I remain open.
